  <steps mode="directional">
    <step>Read the task 121 filing and the engine's status mapping. Write the fail-before tests: a save to the record a Suggested row already points at leaves it Suggested today (red); the unfiled path's resulting status; `derivePrimaryReview` on the fixture shows "requires-review" with no primary today (red).</step>
    <step>Server: confirm (Resolved) after the caller's Write check when the primary regarding is the save's record; fail closed; report the outcome. Decide on the unfiled path, with evidence.</step>
    <step>Client: `derivePrimaryReview` gives a written regarding a primary in 'needs-confirmation'. Run the Spaarke.Communication.Components tests and its consumers' typecheck.</step>
    <step>Diagnose the empty candidates; fix in scope or report.</step>
    <step>Gates: BFF build (0 warnings), the affected BFF test classes and ArchTests (full), Communication.Components jest + typecheck + ESLint/Prettier, office-addins jest if `SaveResponse` handling changed, publish delta, vulnerable packages.</step>
  </steps>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An Office save to record M, where the existing communication is Suggested and its primary regarding is M, leaves it Resolved, after a Write check as the caller on that communication.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">If that Write check refuses or faults, the communication is unchanged, and the save still succeeds and reports the outcome.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: a communication filed to a different record N is neither moved nor confirmed by a save to M.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: an already Resolved communication gets no extra write.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The unfiled-then-filed path's final status is decided with evidence, and tested.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`derivePrimaryReview` on a Suggested row with a written regarding and no candidates returns 'needs-confirmation' with that record as primary. A row with no regarding written still returns 'requires-review'. An Ambiguous conflict still stays red.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The empty-candidates cause is stated with file:line, and fixed with a test or reported with a failure scenario.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <justification>
    <existing>Modifies the existing task 121 filing (`ReconciledEmailFiling`), `derivePrimaryReview`, and possibly the `SaveResponse` outcome values.</existing>
    <extension>Extends them, reusing the panel's existing confirm write and status code; no new route, column or service.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>An email the user explicitly filed from Outlook stays in Needs Review as "No confident match". A reviewer may file it again, or accept the pending create-new-record proposal and make a duplicate record.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <notes>Done 2026-11-26. PR #3214 merged 152397ab11. Empty candidates: SerializeProvenance dropped all candidates/signals past the 10,000-char column (fixed). Two adversarial passes (opus); uac-r2 condition: Resolved drives ThreadContinuityRung auto-file of every regarding, so a save confirms only when the picked record is the SOLE regarding and the pair type is written (RequirePairType), else NotConfirmable → FiledUnconfirmed (pane notice). Dev BFF live in 6a2a569ac9 (uac-r2 gate PASS); Console auto-deploy, sprk_communicationreconciliation and sprk_emailpage verified byte-identical to master. Owner live check PASS. Follow-up ISS-044 #3202 (upload capture on an auto-file-off tenant).</notes>
